---
# Pragmatic level per docs/NAMING.md — Platform/LittleFs.
#
# Inherits the root .clang-tidy. SolidSyslogLittleFsFile.h (Interface/) and the
# sources refer to upstream LittleFS struct types — `lfs`, `lfs_config`,
# `lfs_info`, `lfs_file_config`, … — because the integrator supplies the mounted
# filesystem and the adapter embeds a file handle. The upstream names are
# snake_case in the `lfs` namespace, which violates the project's StructCase +
# StructPrefix rule, and renaming third-party types is not open to us. Extend
# StructIgnoredRegexp locally so the rule exempts that namespace.
#
# clang-tidy CheckOption values do not merge across the hierarchy — the
# latest-encountered value wins. The pattern below therefore re-states the root
# .clang-tidy whitelist plus the lfs namespace. Keep in sync.
InheritParentConfig: true
CheckOptions:
  - {
      key: readability-identifier-naming.StructIgnoredRegexp,
      value: "^(SolidSyslog|EscapedContext|BlockPresence|OpenHandle|LwipRawDatagramCall|LwipRawDnsResolverCall|LwipRawTcpStreamCall|lfs|lfs_[a-z0-9_]+)$",
    }
